    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d899">

                <pb facs="0905" n="893" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg893"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856D.6176/391: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Emmet</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-08T19:00:00-05:00">March 8, 1937—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. The Department has instructed Am[erican] Embassy London to repeat to you long
                    instruction in regard to visit of representatives of American rubber industry.
                    They are going to The Hague first, arriving about March 9. They wish to talk
                    with the responsible officials of the Netherlands Government. Please assist them
                    in every appropriate way in accordance with Department’s cable to London.</p>
                <p>Your 15, March 5, 5 p.m.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d899-f1"/> Department desires you
                    to make whatever additional representations may seem useful in concert with
                    efforts of Messrs. Viles and Blandin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
